[h1]Flavorium 1.3 — Diseases+ Unoffical Hotfix[/h1]

[i]Compatible with EU5 1.3.* [/i]

[hr][/hr]

This mod is a collection of unoffical hotfixes for the obvious issues with the 1.3 beta. Changes will be removed as they are addressed by paradox.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]What changes[/h2]

[h3]Parliament Agenda Fix[/h3]
fixed the ai chance for the change court language agenda being set to a high tester value 10000 instead of 1 like normal 
[h3]Starting Changes[/h3]
[b]Disease starting resistance: 33% -> 75% [/b] for old world locations+diseases. 
this alone was reducing smallpox deaths by 50-75% when first encountering it.
in observation, disease resistance was reaching a higher 'equilibrium' rapidly with an endemic disease, so it seemed more appropriate to start closer to observed resistence minima in the noise of the endemics.
[h3]Smallpox Disease Changes[/h3]
[list]
[*] [b]mortality rate[/b] uniform_random (0.05,0.3) (17.5% avg) to (0.001, 0.25) (12.5% avg) 
    this is closer to the CDC estimate of the endemic fatality rate I saw online.
[*] slightly reduced r0 spread bases for towns and larger urban locations. this is pretty superficial though, the diseases are still endemic.
[*] commented one of the multipliers in the stganation-chance when-present condition - not sure which they meant to leave, but both seemed like another testing defect.
[*] increased the max stagnation-chance in the when-present condition
[/list]


[h2]What it doesn't change or add[/h2]

[list]
[*] Bubonic plague, great pestilence, or malaria (those have separate vanilla values already accounting for prior exposure)
[*] Anything from the other Flavorium mods
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[i]This is a targeted hotfix while the 1.3 beta is open. Feedback on whether changes feel right is welcome on the discussion page.[/i]
